cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  KOMPOSOS-IV-PHARM: a glass-box drug-repurposing triage tool and its negative
  controls
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it. Please cite the
  underlying data sources (ChEMBL, COSMIC, KEGG, DepMap/PRISM,
  ClinicalTrials.gov) separately — see NOTICE for the full inventory.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hawkins
    given-names: James Ray
repository-code: https://github.com/Jayhawk314/KOMPOSOS-IV-PHARM
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  An auditable triage accelerator over known oncology pharmacology. It ranks
  drug-to-disease repurposing candidates as Drug-Protein-Disease paths, where
  every edge carries provenance and an evidence tier. Its value is auditability
  and speed rather than novelty: it recombines recorded drug-target and
  target-disease facts into a source-linked shortlist of hypotheses, and it does
  not discover biology absent from the literature.

  The repository is offered primarily as a methods artifact. It ships four
  measured negative controls in which the system falsified its own components:
  a protein-embedding similarity layer that made the ranker worse when included;
  a permutation control showing that post-hoc PubMed grounding measures corpus
  density rather than biology (Fisher p=0.28); a categorical horn-composition
  layer that added nothing over ordinary pairwise comparison; and a
  pre-registered adjudication against PRISM Repurposing cell-line viability that
  returned no lineage-selective activity for any candidate.

  It also reports a trial-graveyard finding: across the trials tracked by its
  candidate review, 75% never posted results, every recorded stop reason was
  operational or financial rather than efficacy or safety, and 13 trials have
  posted registry results with no publication of any kind. A novelty signal
  built on literature absence therefore cannot distinguish an unexplored
  hypothesis from a quietly abandoned one.

  Research prototype. Not clinical, translational, or regulatory validation.
keywords:
  - drug repurposing
  - knowledge graph
  - negative controls
  - pre-registration
  - reproducibility
  - meta-research
  - oncology
  - category theory
